{"kind":"request","text":"C3 has one ordering question between section 6 rule 4 and section 6.3. A protocol refusal can name a later judgedAt while the feed and journal reads fail. Rule 4 keeps that request pending until its head is held. Section 6.3 says the request returns with its reason and the client stops. Once Replica.protocol stops it, Replica.read makes no further request, so it can never reach that head.\n\nProposal: the client attempts the answer-head read first, then stops for the protocol refusal. A protocol refusal returns its reason even if that read fails; add that explicit exception to rule 4. The pure status function checks protocol class before the head barrier, and the client stops all sends and timers. This treats the refusal as a fault in the client/service agreement, not an ordinary head-dependent refusal. If rule 4 admits no exception, the alternative is pending with the protocol cause on the stopped client state. Which view does C3 publish? No wire shape changes.","body":{"conditions":"Resolve the protocol refusal whose judgedAt head the replica cannot read before C3 fixes that stop's status.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}